cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ColabChem, please cite it as below, together with the
  methods you used (see the Citation section of the README). The
  references below are the works ColabChem builds on and cites.
title: ColabChem
abstract: >-
  Google Colab notebooks for structure optimization, relaxed scans and
  transition state searches with the UMA machine learning potential, and
  DFT single points with GPU4PySCF, including views of the electrostatic
  potential and molecular orbitals.
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-11-07"
authors:
  - family-names: Chiba
    given-names: Ryuhei
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3492-4159"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RChibaChiba/ColabChem"
url: "https://rchibachiba.github.io/ColabChem/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - machine learning interatomic potential
  - UMA
  - transition state
  - DFT
  - Google Colab
